./files/weekly-report-ja-vol1/WEEKLY-KIT.md:130:**Fix (identical in all 7 JA build dirs; patched `svglib.py` md5 d73e23b365676c3618d7e060b835eb4d in each).** New module constant `SEAM_SLACK = 28` (grid pitch 462 − column width 434). `wrap()` now records pre-kinsoku line widths and, after the oidashi loop, repairs ONLY lines oidashi itself grew past `max_w + SEAM_SLACK`: trailing glyphs are shed to the head of the next line until the line fits `max_w` again (cascading forward; a NO_START glyph is shed together with the preceding glyph so no line starts with one). No content string changed; no other wrap result in the issue changes (verified below).
